cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it as below."
title: "quantum-exercises: hands-on Qiskit exercises, from an empty laptop to real IBM hardware"
abstract: >-
  A command line course of seventeen exercises in quantum computing with Qiskit,
  taking a learner from an unprepared machine to a circuit executed on real IBM
  hardware, and on to a CHSH test that exceeds the classical bound. Answers are verified by inspecting the Qiskit objects a learner's
  code produces rather than by comparing source text or program output: states
  and operators are compared up to global phase, and measurement counts are
  tested against statistical tolerances derived from the binomial standard error
  and a chi-square goodness-of-fit test, never for equality. Each submission runs
  in a separate process, and failures are reported in the language of the
  problem rather than as a Python traceback. Every reference solution is re-run
  on the 1st and the 15th of each month against the current Qiskit release, so
  the material cannot rot silently as the library changes.
